<?xml version="1.0"?>
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Config:etc/system_file.xsd">
    <system>
        <tab id="printess" translate="label" sortOrder="500">
            <label>Printess</label>
        </tab>
        <section id="printess_designer" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="100" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
            <label>Printess Editor</label>
            <tab>printess</tab>
            <resource>Printess_PrintessEditor::config</resource>
            <group id="api_token" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>API Settings</label>
                <field id="shop_token" translate="label" type="obscure" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Shop Token (Frontend)</label>
                    <comment>Used in the browser to load the editor. Find it in the Printess account menu under API-Token.</comment>
                    <backend_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Backend\Encrypted</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="service_token" translate="label" type="obscure" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Service Token (Backend / PDF Production)</label>
                    <comment>Used server-side to trigger production. Never expose this in the browser.</comment>
                    <backend_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Backend\Encrypted</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="api_url" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>API URL</label>
                    <comment>Address of the Printess API. Leave blank for https://api.printess.com; only change this if Printess support asks you to.</comment>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="editor" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Editor Appearance</label>
                <field id="theme" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Editor Theme</label>
                    <source_model>Printess\PrintessEditor\Model\Config\Source\EditorTheme</source_model>
                    <comment>Default theme for all Printess editors in this store. Can be overridden per product.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="editor_version" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Editor Version</label>
                    <comment>Which build of the Printess editor to load, e.g. "nightly" for the current staging build. The "/v/" prefix is added automatically if you leave it out. Leave blank to load the current release version.</comment>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="production" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Production</label>
                <field id="print_settings" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Print Settings</label>
                    <source_model>Printess\PrintessEditor\Model\Config\Source\PrintSettings</source_model>
                    <comment>Select the named print settings to use when producing PDFs. Options are loaded from your Printess account.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="hold_until_payment" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Hold Until Paid</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Wait until the order item is invoiced before sending it to production. Applies to all Printess items, including dropshipped ones.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="approve_before_production" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Approve Before Production</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>When enabled, Printess items wait on the order page until an admin approves them. Nothing is produced or shipped before that.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="callback_mode" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="55" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Production Status Updates</label>
                    <source_model>Printess\PrintessEditor\Model\Config\Source\ProductionCallbackMode</source_model>
                    <comment>How the shop learns that production finished and that dropship items shipped. Callbacks: Printess calls this store's own URL right away. If that URL is not publicly reachable over https (e.g. a local or test shop), the shop falls back to polling automatically. Polling: the shop checks Printess every few minutes.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="production_callback_url" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="60" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Callback URL (override, for debugging)</label>
                    <backend_model>Printess\PrintessEditor\Model\Config\Backend\CallbackUrl</backend_model>
                    <depends><field id="callback_mode">callbacks</field></depends>
                    <comment>Leave empty on live shops — Printess then calls this store's own URL. Set it only when Printess can't reach that URL, e.g. a local shop behind an HTTP tunnel. Must be https with a public domain name (no IP addresses or localhost).</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="send_shipment_email" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="70" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Send Shipment Email</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Email the customer the shipment confirmation with tracking information when the dropshipper reports an item as shipped.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="dropship_reproduction_mode" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="80" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Reproducing Dropship Orders</label>
                    <source_model>Printess\PrintessEditor\Model\Config\Source\DropshipReproductionMode</source_model>
                    <comment>Some dropshippers (e.g. Siteflow) refuse an order number they have received before. By default a reproduction is sent under the order number with a suffix. Alternatively you can be asked each time whether to duplicate the order instead: the copy gets a new order number, is free for the customer (a discount line makes the total 0) and carries a message the customer sees.</comment>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="projects" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="40"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Saved Projects and Notifications</label>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Enable expiry reminders and removal of expired Printess projects.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="retention_days" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="20"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Project Retention Days</label>
                    <validate>validate-number validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                    <comment>Number of days a saved project is retained before being deleted. Should align with the save-token expiry set in your Printess account settings.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="order_reminder_after_days" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="30"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Remind to Order After Days</label>
                    <validate>validate-number validate-zero-or-greater</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                    <comment>Send an order reminder email this many days after a project is saved without being ordered. Leave blank to disable order reminders entirely. Minimum 1 day.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="removal_reminder_before_days" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="40"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Removal Reminder Before Days</label>
                    <validate>validate-number validate-zero-or-greater</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                    <comment>Send a project deletion warning email this many days before the project expires. Leave blank to disable removal reminders entirely. Minimum 1 day.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="order_reminder_template" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="50"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Remind to Order Email Template</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Email\Template</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                    <comment>Email template sent to customers who have a saved project but have not yet placed an order.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="removal_reminder_template" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="60"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Removal Reminder Email Template</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Email\Template</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                    <comment>Email template sent to customers warning that their saved project is about to be permanently deleted.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="email_batch_limit" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="70"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Email Send Batch Limit</label>
                    <validate>validate-number validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                    <comment>Maximum reminders sent by each cron run.</comment>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="supervisor_approval" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="50" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Supervisor Approval</label>
                <comment>Designs of customers must be approved by a Supervisor before they can be ordered. Supervisors are storefront customers with "Printess Supervisor" = Yes (Customers → All Customers → Edit). Supervisor status is website wide.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Supervisor Feedback on orders</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>When enabled, "Add to basket" becomes "Submit for approval" and only approved designs can be added to the cart. Customers must be logged in.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="default_supervisor" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Default Order Supervisor</label>
                    <source_model>Printess\PrintessEditor\Model\Config\Source\Supervisors</source_model>
                    <backend_model>Printess\PrintessEditor\Model\Config\Backend\DefaultSupervisor</backend_model>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                    <comment>Notified about new submissions. A product can override this (product attribute "Default Order Supervisor"). With no supervisor set, all supervisors of the website are notified. Every supervisor of the website can review every submission.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="supervisors_need_approval" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Supervisors' Own Designs Need Approval</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                    <comment>No: supervisors order their own designs directly. Yes: another supervisor must approve them (nobody can approve their own design).</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="edit_lock_minutes" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Supervisor Edit Lock (minutes)</label>
                    <validate>validate-number validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                    <comment>While a supervisor edits a design, other supervisors cannot act on it for this long.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="notify_on_retract" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="50" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Notify Supervisor When a Design Is Retracted</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="email_identity" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="100" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Email Sender</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Email\Identity</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="template_submitted" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="110" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Email Template: Submitted</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Email\Template</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="template_changes_requested" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="120" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Email Template: Changes requested</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Email\Template</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="template_supervisor_changed" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="130" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Email Template: Supervisor changed</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Email\Template</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="template_approved" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="140" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Email Template: Approved</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Email\Template</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="template_accepted" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="150" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Email Template: Accepted</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Email\Template</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="template_replied" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="160" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Email Template: Replied</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Email\Template</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="template_retracted" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="170" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Email Template: Retracted</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Email\Template</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="template_comment" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="180" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Email Template: Comment</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Email\Template</source_model>
                    <depends><field id="enabled">1</field></depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="login_popup" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="60" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Login Popup Headings</label>
                <comment>Text shown in the authentication popup when a guest clicks the Personalise button.</comment>
                <field id="new_customer_heading" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>New Customer Heading</label>
                    <comment>Overrides the "New Customers" heading in the registration panel. Leave blank to use the default theme text.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="customer_login_heading" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Customer Login Heading</label>
                    <comment>Overrides the "Registered Customers" heading in the login panel. Leave blank to use the default theme text.</comment>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="display" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="70" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Friendly Option Display</label>
                <field id="friendly_option_labels" translate="label comment" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Friendly Option Labels</label>
                    <frontend_model>Printess\PrintessEditor\Block\Adminhtml\Form\Field\FriendlyOptionLabelRule</frontend_model>
                    <backend_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Backend\Serialized\ArraySerialized</backend_model>
                    <comment>
                        Override how raw product option labels/values are displayed in cart, checkout and order
                        emails, without changing the underlying option data. Leave "Option Value" blank to relabel
                        the option itself (e.g. DOCUMENT_SIZE -&gt; Document Size); fill it in to relabel one
                        specific value of that option (e.g. COVER_TYPE / HC -&gt; Hard Cover).
                    </comment>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
    </system>
</config>
